The primary objective of the Supply Chain & Warehouse Logistics Network Management System is to provide a centralized, 
robust relational database platform to track inventory across multiple geographically distributed warehouses, manage supplier purchasing workflows, 
monitor multi-stage shipment logistics, and support multi-level component assembly operations. 

Specifically, the system addresses key operational capabilities:

-Multi-Warehouse Inventory Visibility: Tracking real-time stock levels of products across different physical locations. 
-Automated Restock Threshold Tracking: Monitoring stock levels against predefined minimum reorder thresholds to trigger inventory replenishment. 
-Bill of Materials (BOM) Management: Supporting recursive structures where complex products are assembled from sub-components. 
-End-to-End Logistics Tracking: Managing supplier purchase orders and tracking shipments between source and destination warehouses. 
